":["The Death of Saint Bruno is a 1645–1648 oil on canvas painting by Eustache Lesueur, the last in a cycle of 22 paintings of episodes from the life of Bruno of Cologne produced for the walls of the minor cloister of the couvent des Chartreux in Paris and in 1776 offered to Louis XVI by the Couvent.","The Death of Saint Bruno"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}